---
/**
 * /work — a short landing page, then three cards linking out.
 *
 * No photograph here. The closing block reads as an invitation, not a pitch: a
 * recruiter should get through the page without anything smelling of a funnel,
 * and a client who is nodding needs an address, not a booking widget.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import Doors from '../../components/Doors.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const cards = [
	{
		href: '/work/essays',
		kicker: 'Writing',
		title: 'Essays',
		line: 'Brands, culture and behaviour. What I\'d want to be read.',
	},
	{
		href: '/work/ai-adoption',
		kicker: 'Case study',
		title: 'AI Adoption: a case study',
		line: 'A workflow-first adoption course for working professionals. I wrote up what happened in the room as a case study on adoption behaviour.',
	},
	{
		href: '/work/ai-workshops',
		kicker: 'Teaching',
		title: 'AI Workshops',
		line: 'Generative AI for working professionals at the Volkshochschulen in Berlin.',
	},
];

const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---

<PageLayout
	title="Work"
	description="Branding, communications and marketing, across consumer tech, fintech, B2B consulting and industry."
	quiet
>
	<section class="section section--flush">
		<div class="shell">
			<Prose class="prose--plain prose--split">
				<h2>What I do</h2>
				<p>
					Most communication problems aren’t writing problems. They’re problems of not knowing what the
					other side already thinks.
				</p>
				<p>Things I'm usually hired for:</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Branding and positioning.</strong> Working out what an organisation actually stands
					for, in language it can use, and keeping it consistent as the business changes underneath it.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Strategic communications.</strong> Internal and external messaging through change —
					transformations, launches, the moments when what you say matters more than usual. Including
					the unglamorous parts: all-hands scripts, incident comms, the email that has to go out before
					the rumour does.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Thought leadership and executive communications.</strong> Op-eds, keynotes, LinkedIn,
					bylines. With the editorial strategy and channel planning behind them, so it isn’t one good
					piece followed by eight months of silence.
				</p>

				<h2>Where I've done it</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>Siemens Advanta, Munich.</strong> Communication and content strategy for digital
					transformation propositions, with product, sales and leadership.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>SWISS KRONO, Berlin.</strong> Group communications across internal channels, website
					and social, during a period of transformation.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Times Internet, India.</strong> Organic social and communications for co-branded card
					products with HDFC Bank. Before that, customer experience for a product with 300,000 daily
					active users.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>MakeMyTrip, India.</strong> Four years coordinating product, sales, finance and
					suppliers in high-volume travel operations.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Volkshochschule, Berlin.</strong> Generative AI for working professionals, using
					frameworks I built. The closest thing I have to a live research setting.
				</p>
			</Prose>


			<Prose class="prose--plain prose--split open justify">
				<p>
					I'm open to communications and branding roles in Germany, and to consulting and collaboration
					alongside them. If you have something in mind, write to me at{' '}
					<a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>. I answer everything.
				</p>
			</Prose>

			<div class="split split--wide cards">
				<div class="split__body">
					<Doors items={cards} label="Work" />
				</div>
			</div>

		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.justify :global(p) {
		text-align: justify;
		hyphens: auto;
	}

	.open {
		margin-block-start: var(--sp-7);
	}

	.cards {
		margin-block: var(--sp-7);
	}
</style>
